+# Hemera no_std feature PLAN evidence
+
+This is a proposed two-line nox manifest repair, with no production change at
+freeze. Parent: `0b1407a4b855e4961ede07e1b7ea199cb8018c30`. The
+[research](../../.claude/tasks/hemera-no-std/research.md) and
+[PLAN](../../.claude/tasks/hemera-no-std/plan.md) distinguish source correction
+from owner-only registry delivery. Fresh Opus PLAN was pending at capsule freeze;
+this audit does not imply implementation or approval.
+
+The 130675-byte readable review input has SHA-256
+`3b17ac27ecf44c2e211f1e87a14f0f914825b53aabac6f488862f9cc701e9ea4`.
+Its 50 sections bind the complete current/proposed manifest, critical source and
+canonical contracts, actual H264 controls and decisive raw results. Full omitted
+support is indexed; it is not claimed read by the vendor. Parent and normalized
+package thumb both fail on Hemera/std. Command 13 reports 161 parent library
+tests passed; locked command 16 reports four real H264 controls passed. This is
+neither full Kadek conformance nor delivery to Kadek's locked registry dependency.
+
+The capsule preserves four exact source archives (536 Git entries), the local
+parent package, published nox archive, 18 command records and 36 full raw streams,
+crate checksum inventory, rejected source-normalization topology, source extraction
+scripts, initial cache-resolution failures and initial packet-encoding failure.
+Exact Git input files and published/current nox source correspondences are checked.
+Dependency cache bodies are not republished wholesale; archive checksums and every
+observed extracted file hash retain the reproducible source requirements.
+
+```sh
+nu audit/2026-10-13-hemera-no-std-plan/verify.nu audit/2026-10-13-hemera-no-std-plan
+```
+
+The permanent verifier requires Nu, tar, gzip, mktemp and read-only Git blob
+hashing. Historical Ruby helpers remain provenance only. It verifies saved bytes,
+source epochs, exact review reconstruction, package/source identity and observed
+outcomes; it does not rerun Cargo or turn pending review into approval. The root's
+independent Git-aware replay result is retained inside the capsule. Broader consumer
+and release obligations, Kadek alloc/math work and publication remain open.
